[{:question/id #uuid "53218be1-6a3c-5560-9338-ef81bd9ab181" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=- \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "cf12cc56-7e9d-5f32-968f-6c8272d67936" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a1c429d-91c5-5bb7-af02-633485681a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id "a-6a1c429d-91c5-5bb7-af02-633485681a8d"}] :answer-field/correct "a-6a1c429d-91c5-5bb7-af02-633485681a8d" :db/id "f-cf12cc56-7e9d-5f32-968f-6c8272d67936"}] :db/id "q-53218be1-6a3c-5560-9338-ef81bd9ab181"} [:db/add 17592186064284 :knowledge-point/questions "q-53218be1-6a3c-5560-9338-ef81bd9ab181"] [:db/ensure "q-53218be1-6a3c-5560-9338-ef81bd9ab181" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-cf12cc56-7e9d-5f32-968f-6c8272d67936" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-6a1c429d-91c5-5bb7